  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837072",
      "title": "Creating Flexible Custom Hooks",
      "sourceHash": "b60120ad748bd4deff7413a66642d136c2d2a2697c53a8f7b71151dcbf4c7644",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.93,
          "end": 2.73,
          "en": "So that all works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.73,
          "end": 6.123,
          "en": "but how can we bring back that sorting logic now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "Well, there definitely are different possible solutions you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "could come up with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "One solution I can think of is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 17.403,
          "en": "to create a separate function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.974,
          "end": 22.143,
          "en": "\"fetchSortedPlaces\" could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.19,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "which should be an async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 29.577,
          "en": "where you start by calling an \"await fetchAvailablePlaces.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "So where we call this function, which we're importing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 39.32,
          "en": "which will yield those places or throw an error if it fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 45.75,
          "en": "That will give us our places, and now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.75,
          "end": 49.833,
          "en": "you could move this code here into this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 55.91,
          "en": "comment it back in, get rid of the state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "and make sure that you return a promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "after you got the current position, and to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 64.41,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "you can return a new promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 70.47,
          "en": "by creating a new promise object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 70.47,
          "end": 73.59,
          "en": "a feature that's built into the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.59,
          "end": 77.43,
          "en": "and this promise constructor function takes a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 82.43,
          "en": "as an argument where you then get two parameters passed in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 86.85300000000001,
          "en": "by the browser, a resolve and a reject parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 88.35,
          "end": 90.33,
          "en": "and in this function body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 90.33,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "you could now execute this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 94.68299999999999,
          "en": "where you fetch the user's location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "By using this promise constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 102.81,
          "en": "we are promisifying this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.81,
          "end": 105.50999999999999,
          "en": "which means we're wrapping it in a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "and we're turning it into a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 112.14,
          "en": "which we need to do because I wanna return a promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.14,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "because useFetch expects the fetch function to yield",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 119.52000000000001,
          "en": "a promise since we're awaiting the result here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "So the fetch function must yield a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 125.103,
          "en": "and that's why I am creating a promise here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "Now, we just make sure that this promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "which I am creating here resolves to a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 136.86,
          "en": "and lets use fetch, know that the wait time is over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.86,
          "end": 138.66,
          "en": "that the value is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.66,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "by calling Resolve once the value is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 146.643,
          "en": "which is the case in here after we have our sorted places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "Here, we need to call Resolve and pass our sorted places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 155.28300000000002,
          "en": "as a resolved value to Resolve,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 159.96,
          "en": "and this will now make sure that when we wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 159.96,
          "end": 164.01,
          "en": "for fetchSortedPlaces, because we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 164.01,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "use this as a fetch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 170.07,
          "en": "it's this value that will in the end be returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.07,
          "end": 173.973,
          "en": "by the overall promise returned by this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "This is not React-specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "Instead, this is a standard JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "and a standard JavaScript pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 188.49,
          "en": "and approach for converting a non-promise feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 191.883,
          "en": "and API into a promise-based feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 192.72,
          "end": 194.88,
          "en": "Now here, I therefore actually don't care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 194.88,
          "end": 196.74,
          "en": "about the Reject feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 196.74,
          "end": 200.97,
          "en": "which I could use to throw an error inside of a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 200.97,
          "end": 203.343,
          "en": "but here, for this case, we can ignore this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 208.65,
          "en": "and it's now this fetchSortedPlaces function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 208.65,
          "end": 212.28300000000002,
          "en": "that should be used as a data-fetching function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 213.12,
          "end": 214.02,
          "en": "fetchSortedPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 219.333,
          "end": 223.44,
          "en": "This function still calls fetchAvailablePlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 223.44,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "but it then also performs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 230.61,
          "en": "this distance-based sorting and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 230.61,
          "end": 233.73,
          "en": "our useFetch hook does not have to change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 236.37,
          "en": "It still calls this fetching function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 238.35,
          "en": "which does all that work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 238.35,
          "end": 240.51,
          "en": "and it's still catches any errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 240.51,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "that might occur during that work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 246.273,
          "en": "and it still updates all these states,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 247.56,
          "end": 250.71,
          "en": "and that's therefore a straightforward solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 252.003,
          "en": "for this problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "Now, I can also get rid of setFetchedData here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 259.14300000000003,
          "en": "because I actually don't need it in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 260.01,
          "end": 262.497,
          "en": "and we can get rid of the useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 262.497,
          "end": 266.553,
          "en": "and useEffect imports because we don't need those either.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "Instead of, you now save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "you should see that we're still fetching those places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 278.55,
          "en": "and we're still sorting them by distance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 278.55,
          "end": 281.52,
          "en": "and if I open the dev tools to check for errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 281.52,
          "end": 283.413,
          "en": "you can tell there are none.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 284.64,
          "end": 289.11,
          "en": "So this works, and of course, adding places still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 289.11,
          "end": 293.67,
          "en": "reloading works, removing places works, that all works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 297.993,
          "en": "and it now all works powered by a custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
